{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372607Z","id":"94ab5cdaf4de5bbed63a3fac96b1c4d50f4102b26fc9a41c5430dbdc8a8c63ea","body":{"detail":"The header says Clax has no guests; a hosted instance has them, and `me()` answers isOwner and canEdit from env.token alone, so a hosted guest reads as a member and a member with publish rights as unable to edit. The server enforces the rights, so a page cannot gain anything by it, but a page that trusts these fields misbehaves.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"755f77437e4c357f9c227a909b248314d87a2588d394fbdfe8c65d3a5fbd33f8"},"suggested_fix":"Carry the hosted viewer's guest flag and rights in CapEnv.viewer and answer from them.","summary":"The user capability tells pages guest: false and computes isOwner and canEdit from the shell token, which is wrong on a hosted instance","tags":["hosted","web","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441126Z","id":"aee18f03f11cc59b3612e2806bf5b1c4e85aada60b8ee03d1138f7923e72154c","body":{"detail":"While the daemon answers the stream but a single refetch times out, the source app's snapshot can stay stale until B's next change or the stream's next ready. The page's own db subscriptions retry after RETRY_MS and poll every POLL_MS while the stream is down; port that logic here if stale cross-app snapshots show up in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"2ffc45b02bf3af4d3477b6835de2a5b2a2620f01f4c8151e6494bf761bb59040"},"summary":"A db.artifact(id) subscription whose refetch fails unavailable waits for the next doc event, ready or resync: no retry backoff and no outage poll, unlike the page's own subscriptions in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts (RETRY_MS, POLL_MS)","tags":["W3","deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441196Z","id":"b72b4452c404f6ccd348755aca31f83791badd26f971526c693b56747202a81c","body":{"detail":"The bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts makeDb, active set) counts both kinds against one 64 for an honest page; a page that talks to the shell directly can hold 64 of each. Each source app adds one stream topic (docs:<B>?reader=<A>), bounded by db.read's 16 IDs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"511d681aca548961bc00b3b9c4675e6f2f722ebdd8950507cadc8cd4a965e31f"},"summary":"Subscriptions to other apps are capped at MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS on their own, beside the page's own cap in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts, so the shell holds up to 2 x 64 per view","tags":["W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441224Z","id":"44415b8019adb146027a3212e7d0baa2bff4da3e64410a6d1c46acd767d5882e","body":{"detail":"The `asked` map (line 45) keeps one answer per source per CapabilityHost. Refetches of a live subscription never ask (read(..., mayAsk=false)), so a grant revoked while the page runs ends the subscription with not_granted instead of raising a dialog.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"5795cbafe3c3447f007acfbeca9b3951ba185d746a88c65b910411aca71ecd64"},"summary":"The consent dialog's dismissal (Escape, outside click) counts as Don't allow for the rest of the view: db.artifact(id) reads of that source reject not_granted without asking again until the view reloads","tags":["W3","design","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717816Z","id":"ab8293dbb08f5e751602871afbff28870fe0b27f70578915c11124f1fddbc01a","body":{"detail":"subscribe tests subs.size >= MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS (line 192), then awaits current() (line 195), then subs.set (line 197). A page that posts many db.read subscribe calls with distinct sub IDs at once (the bridge's own 64 cap, web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts active set, is bypassed by posting to the shell directly) gets every one: a scratch vitest firing 200 concurrent {op: 'subscribe', artifact: B, sub: 's<i>', spec: {kind: 'doc', path: 'runs/r1'}} against crossRead with an allowing fetch saw 200 fulfilled. Each one then refetches B on every matching doc event and on every ready/resync, so the page can make the daemon serve unbounded reads of B per change. The bound stated in b72b4452 (2 x 64 per view) does not hold. The consent boundary is unaffected: every request still carries the view's reader and checked paths.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:647958f22844","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"dcc42c3d61ccaa46b8a4fa1963bfc181995cfbcfd287a2c86cf5eb46be153662"},"suggested_fix":"Count in-flight subscribes against the cap: reserve the sub ID in a pending set synchronously before the await (and release it on failure), or check the cap again after the await and refuse resource_exhausted.","summary":"The cross-read subscription cap is checked before the consent read is awaited and the subscription is stored after it, so concurrent subscribe calls all pass the check: one view can hold any number of db.artifact(id) subscriptions","tags":["review","W3","resources","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717913Z","id":"5a524b375e1b90d8279ea19926d4d63da8e63cfc9e84e1a7255ab3ed9ba1a702","body":{"detail":"reset/leave run endAll over subs (line 171), but a subscribe awaiting its first read (line 195) is not yet in subs; when it resolves it checks only disposed (line 196), then subs.set, watch(topicOf(src)) and env.post. A scratch vitest calling subscribe, then cr.reset(), then awaiting the subscribe saw the watch still live and one snapshot posted. The subscription then lives until the next reset or dispose, refetching B for a document that never asked for it. The page's own subscriptions in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts store the spec synchronously before the await (subscribe case), so reset drops them; the consent wait makes the cross-read path different. Same artifact and same consent, so no data crosses the boundary.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:647958f22844","span":{"start":{"line":193},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"05989561585165651b921fc91bc9938aed62503aeea76cd2bc067f1b3bd202e1"},"suggested_fix":"Give crossRead a generation counter bumped by reset/leave; subscribe captures it before the await and, when it changed, returns without storing, watching or posting (rejecting unavailable).","summary":"A db.artifact(id) subscribe still in flight when the frame loads a new document (reset) or leaves survives it: it stores the subscription, follows the reader topic and posts snapshots into the next document","tags":["review","W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.718005Z","id":"ea15c9e5c9f2590039bf79c6a45ac5921794c63b8b99a90f3ccee87f8b986d99","body":{"detail":"get maps the daemon's not_declared (B's declaration lacks db) to not_granted (line 77); read (line 107) then prompts the owner in the owner shell. Allow PUTs the grant and the retried read is refused again. The page sees not_granted either way, but the owner is shown 'Let A read B's data?' for an app with no documents to share.","kind":"suggestion","ref":"git:647958f22844","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"4ecc5ee6b708ab584a2b2481fc208b736c63543fefe679db25496a86eb1e926a"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the daemon's not_declared as a separate internal signal that rejects not_granted without asking.","summary":"A source that does not declare db answers not_declared, which the shell turns into not_granted and so asks the owner for a grant that cannot make the read succeed","tags":["review","W3","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.892605Z","id":"23969f0e7fac4d3578914886f92fa213c1afdb2d9471142e5c6cdf4f99babbd2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"subscribe stores its entry before the first await (cross-read.ts subscribe case), so the cap counts pending subscriptions; 'holds at most MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS subscriptions of other apps, however many are asked for at once' fires 200 concurrent subscribes: 64 fulfilled, 136 resource_exhausted, one watch (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"ab8293dbb08f5e751602871afbff28870fe0b27f70578915c11124f1fddbc01a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.892995Z","id":"46cd769037cb3a9531777f91f979812a8ec1e78b0905bd4bb93c4ff90dd4af40","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Each subscribe holds its own entry object as its token; reset, leave and unsubscribe remove it, and the subscribe rejects unavailable when its entry is no longer the one under its ID. 'drops a subscribe still waiting on its first read when the frame resets or leaves' checks no watch and no snapshot for both reset and leave (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"5a524b375e1b90d8279ea19926d4d63da8e63cfc9e84e1a7255ab3ed9ba1a702","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893592Z","id":"a790ad4605cc9bb0cd4f2ed5e21b0a07c26a9e2643d8c231e91e558ae324c1a1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The daemon's not_declared stays not_declared, and ask() reads the source's declaration (GET /api/artifacts/<B>) and throws not_declared without a dialog when it lacks db. 'keeps not_declared from a source without db, and never asks for a grant that cannot help' covers granted and ungranted readers: no prompt, no PUT (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"ea15c9e5c9f2590039bf79c6a45ac5921794c63b8b99a90f3ccee87f8b986d99","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893919Z","id":"987f6cee41694dc9159b8de6b5802bf64b228f61e338ffffa65037ea521af7d9","body":{"detail":"The slot is reserved synchronously before the consent read (subscribe case), so concurrent calls cannot pass the cap. The bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts makeDb, active set) counts both kinds against one 64 for an honest page. Each source app adds one stream topic (docs:<B>?reader=<A>), bounded by db.read's 16 IDs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":205},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"511d681aca548961bc00b3b9c4675e6f2f722ebdd8950507cadc8cd4a965e31f"},"summary":"Subscriptions to other apps are capped at MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS (64) per view, pending ones included, beside the page's own 64 in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts: at most 128 per view for a page that posts to the shell directly","supersedes":"b72b4452c404f6ccd348755aca31f83791badd26f971526c693b56747202a81c","tags":["W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697744Z","id":"3b606a25e7e8e69af41b80a969976d6569a8e0f8a5ff6307ed964a2a2c8898c5","body":{"detail":"Failure: /a/<id>?app=1 with claxHost.init and enterCommentMode(); attestPointer({pointer:1,phase:'down'}) at the press, touchStart on #p, held 600 ms, eight touchMoves over 600 ms, touchEnd, then attestPointer({phase:'up'}) as the app's runJavaScript delivers it after the WebView's touchend: clax:pick has clipError 'it was not taken'. With the same drag and the 'up' attested before touchEnd, or with a drag of under ~400 ms after the 600 ms hold, the pick is taken with quote 'Grow revenue in eve'. comment-mode.ts touchDragEnd picks synchronously on touchend, and the shell evaluates frameGesture() on clax:pick-start at once (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts), so the press attestation is stale (HOLD_MS 450 + any real drag > 550 ms) and the release attestation races the frame's postMessage. The long-press no-click fallback is safe only because it waits TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS (400 ms) before picking. Whether Android WebView or WKWebView deliver the host's runJavaScript before the frame's message is unspecified.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"bd2ebcc88bd125d75f7944555c16b23a2bcb14862d119370e7152be524e71591"},"suggested_fix":"Do not depend on the order: in app mode let a pick start wait briefly (bounded, e.g. up to 300 ms on the test clock) for a pending release attestation of a pointer in `pressed`, or count an attested press as fresh until its release is attested (pressed set non-empty) rather than for ATTEST_MS from the press. Cover both orders in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts.","summary":"In app mode a hold-then-drag lasting over ATTEST_MS (1 s, press to release) is refused unless the host's 'up' attestation reaches the shell before the bridge's pick start","tags":["review","touch","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:31.119092Z","id":"c8f75caa789a864c7c070305475af005bd833849acf093d315f08fb6748aef56","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: an attested press counts until its paired release (plus ATTEST_MS after it, at most HELD_MAX_MS while held), and a pick start with no counted arrival waits PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS (300 ms) for a pending release attestation. Evidence: web/e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts app mode, a 600 ms hold plus a 600 ms drag with the 'up' attested after touchEnd, and with it before, and a quick drag: pick taken, no clipError; an unattested drag still gets 'it was not taken' (12 passed). Unit: web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'takes a slow hold-then-drag's pick whose release is attested after the pick starts', 'lets a pick start wait PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS ...', 'starts no wait without a pending press ...' (56 passed).","supersedes":"3b606a25e7e8e69af41b80a969976d6569a8e0f8a5ff6307ed964a2a2c8898c5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:21:40.604253Z","id":"8454afd70754be6bf452b46bb98f3892e79c4e635e66266fe18584e43f377730","body":{"detail":"Grants are per artifact ID (crates/clax-core/src/store/net_grants.rs), and the app's draft (spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design §5.1) has its own ID that the owner never grants: the inspect view answers every prompt \"Don't allow\" (web/shell/src/app/host.ts closeForInspect) and this handler does not ask there. So an app whose first screen fetches renders its error state for the agent, and tests that need the network fail. Letting a draft use its app's grant (draft_of) would expose fetched data to the agent, as cross-read refuses to (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs may_read); a canned or recorded response for drafts is the other route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"5db7b3e3c29aa7382885c61ad7e0f6615564070f0db6e4ea6dee89919103f833"},"summary":"A draft never fetches: its render and tests see not_granted for every net call","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/sample.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:22:28.235145Z","id":"295a31f61e5b2b0551c128efd4bd83022fa20dd5760aa9bd1418d270358730b0","body":{"detail":"Consent uses the shell's own dialog (Grants.request through env.prompt), the path the cross-read consent takes in app mode. No device or Flutter run has shown the sample dialog yet. In the agent's inspect render (?app=1&inspect=1, a hidden WebView) a draft has no grant (grants are per artifact ID, crates/clax-core/src/store/sample_grants.rs), so a page that calls sample() at load would wait on a dialog nobody sees until the inspection's answer limit; cross-read refuses without asking there (web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts header).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"e3431c6db0fd04375fc37b0e7bf4b6ba366ed5ddf0fa338524e6d7e27d9b338b"},"summary":"The per-app sample consent dialog is unverified inside the Flutter app's chromeless app mode and in the agent's inspect render","tags":["unverified","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/sample.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:22:28.235213Z","id":"77b47ff08058a2f8e5f9458d0565cd9c6667f5fca3ad7f6e15c7ae101029cadf","body":{"detail":"The daemon's grant (migration 27) now applies to every client of a daemon, so the desktop shell also asks once per app instead of at each view's first call (the 0.2.61 sample.d.ts wording). One rule is simpler, the grant is revocable over /api/artifacts/{aid}/sample-grant, and the desktop daemon also gets the $0.50 default cost cap. Keeping per-view consent on desktop would need the shell to know it is in the app (?app=1) and the daemon to accept calls without a grant from other views.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"e3431c6db0fd04375fc37b0e7bf4b6ba366ed5ddf0fa338524e6d7e27d9b338b"},"summary":"Per-view sample consent kept for the desktop browser, per-app only in the phone app","tags":["revisit:the owner wants desktop pages to ask at every view again","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:24:45.782256Z","id":"56a60672d7677067fc691e418ef7049d4bfbd44acb36b91ba87d3de645d801fe","body":{"detail":"ask() shows the hosts of the view's own declaration (env.declared, and past three only 'and N more'), then PUT /api/artifacts/<aid>/net-grants with no body; Store::grant_net (crates/clax-core/src/store/net_grants.rs:84-110) grants every host the live version declares at that moment. A version published between the view's load and the owner's Allow, or a view of an older version, gets hosts the owner never saw granted; with more than three hosts the owner never sees the rest even in the normal case. NetAccess::allows still requires the live declaration, so this is a consent gap, not a fetch outside the declaration.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":79},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"33c77d33c421017197d25baa22f72c5e1d313096f60bd10e76f96f0f94c37012"},"suggested_fix":"PUT {hosts:[...]} with the list the dialog showed (all of it, not truncated); grant_net grants only hosts in both that list and the live declaration, and answers granted:false when the live list has more.","summary":"Allow grants the live version's hosts, not the hosts the owner was shown","tags":["review","N1","security","consent","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/sample.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:25:13.963489Z","id":"0e0234e44836e45495b239d05376ad3394775f183785bc8fc460200611630382","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"295a31f61e5b2b0551c128efd4bd83022fa20dd5760aa9bd1418d270358730b0","summary":"The inspect-render half holds: web/shell/src/app/host.ts:407-415 (closeForInspect) answers every consent prompt Don't allow without showing it, so sample() in a draft's render rejects not_granted at once rather than waiting; host.test.ts:1161 covers the generic prompt. The chromeless app mode half stays unverified.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/sample.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:25:14.000494Z","id":"4c5b61b40e4449d9da63494b665eb66d12df3948dd2bf196fc3d8b21913df434","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts:124 and cross-read.ts:124 check inspectQuery and have tests (net.test.ts:94, cross-read.test.ts:120); sample.ts relies on host.ts closeForInspect answering the grants prompt deny, and sample.test.ts has no inspect case. A change to closeForInspect or to the prompt path would let a draft's render wait on a hidden dialog until the inspector's settle and per-test timeouts (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/inspector.dart:21,35).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"44a87a1e9e4507a9b3e3bee26822a3d837678885d0d93964c01158bead6dbb96"},"suggested_fix":"Add a sample.test.ts case at ?app=1&inspect=1 asserting run() rejects not_granted and grants.request shows nothing, or short-circuit with inspectQuery like net.ts.","summary":"No test pins that sample() in the app's inspect view rejects not_granted without asking","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:29:56.983688Z","id":"456c57dc739bdf47f7f947ccd4e9abbe6434df6eae874bc066055f8c9d925013","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The prompt lists every declared host (its text scrolls, theme.css #prompt-body, 647958f22844) and PUTs {hosts} with that list; Store::grant_net grants only hosts in both the list and the live declaration. Passing: store::net_grants::tests::only_the_shown_hosts_that_are_declared_are_granted, api_net::a_fetch_needs_the_owners_grant_and_ends_with_its_revocation, shell/src/caps/net.test.ts 'shows every host it asks for', e2e/net.spec.ts 'a long host list is shown whole' (3 passed).","supersedes":"56a60672d7677067fc691e418ef7049d4bfbd44acb36b91ba87d3de645d801fe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/db.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:50:35.449473Z","id":"3a442a1579211295a2f7c67cf0bc5839d8b29215e138f6abc8dddfe21b2de09e","body":{"detail":"Every db handle the page can reach in the migration view goes through this handler (the page's window.claude.use('db') proxies to the shell), and the artifact frame's CSP blocks fetch (connect-src 'none'), so the known paths are covered. Not covered: a write path outside this handler (a form POST or navigation to the Docs routes, the room or artifact capabilities if they ever write documents, a future db method added without calling journal()). Such a write would not be undone by a rollback of data/users/. Any new db write method must call journal() first.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"08d9ae211ca18fd40bad393fddcb32e27afef777261395542017fcf8feae833f"},"summary":"The migration journal covers writes made through the shell's db handler only; a hostile migrate.js that found another write path would go unjournaled","tags":["security","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989555Z","id":"c86eceaa05f4532f5e2a0ac58425e79d0650dae5a2c41327be5b37be1713edba","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8454afd70754be6bf452b46bb98f3892e79c4e635e66266fe18584e43f377730","summary":"The kit's map (apps/clax_app/assets/kit/map.js) meets this too: in the agent's renders of a draft every tile is not_granted, so the map shows its 'Map tiles need permission' note instead of tiles, and the agent sees no map until the app is published and allowed.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:35:45.371490Z","id":"8de1c89ad25c3616f9c66d06f528f09fa24f76d3bcaef002900bcefb4d4ceb0e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"A draft now fetches under its live app's existing net grants (crates/clax-core/src/store/net_grants.rs access_in), for hosts both the draft and the live app declare, never asking and never granted itself; a new app's draft stays not_granted. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server api_net::a_draft_fetches_under_its_live_apps_grants and -p clax-core net_grants::tests::a_draft_uses_its_live_apps_grants_for_hosts_both_declare pass (1297 tests run: 1297 passed across clax-core and clax-server).","supersedes":"8454afd70754be6bf452b46bb98f3892e79c4e635e66266fe18584e43f377730","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/device.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:05:34.044431Z","id":"01c684b62958bd14de1cdfbf67f40c5adb2f4a820b16d813e2c9679aa8fdbb35","body":{"detail":"The gate is frameGesture() (line 73), which holds while navigator.userActivation.isActive (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:548-554), about 5 s after the last tap in the page in Chromium, and the call does not consume it. A tap on the location pill (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:751-763) is Flutter input the WebView never sees, so it neither ends nor resets that activation. A page that starts a watch from a tap and, on the 'stopped' end, calls watch again succeeds if the person stopped it within those seconds, and the pill comes straight back. One activation also starts up to 4 watches (DeviceHost.maxWatches) and any number of location.current calls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"1ad4881487b318338fa2de3c1010aedc0dc1c230613920ffcdebb58ff36a614c"},"suggested_fix":"Have DeviceHost refuse a watch start for a view until the page sees a gesture newer than the last stop (the app knows the pill tap and stopWatches times; the host can attest the next press on the frame), or consume the activation on a watch start.","summary":"A page can start location.watch again right after the person stops it with the pill, on the activation left from its earlier tap","tags":["review","l1","privacy","location","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/device.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:25:23.363970Z","id":"53cd943ea51500591fb0d69733f770fa4cfaac7f633cc358c93f5b212b372788","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: location.current and location.watch each need a host-attested press (hostArrival.presses) newer than the one the last location call used and newer than a watch's end. web: npx vitest run shell/src/caps/device.test.ts, 'a location call spends the tap: one press starts one, and after a watch ends a new press is needed' passes.","supersedes":"01c684b62958bd14de1cdfbf67f40c5adb2f4a820b16d813e2c9679aa8fdbb35","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/home.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359648Z","id":"8c0474a591dec873f4f12c9de344c24d360108999d04787bba9ab82248bb9a52","body":{"detail":"deviceLink.events gets the home listener when CapabilityHost first calls the lazy handler (web/shell/src/caps/lazy.ts). A page that only calls home.on before any call hears nothing; the contract (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts Home.on) says so, and a page reading apps() first is unaffected since each event carries the whole latest value.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"7192452fc8f36250b016a6e88a47f12adf39e460838d9f0de59ecc0ad0b50eca"},"summary":"home events reach the page only after its first home call: the handler that forwards them is loaded lazily on that call","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/home.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:03:24.715807Z","id":"12f1ebe430aba5433b13cd0cb04e2489a4265b6418b7910950b1d562dc1163c8","body":{"detail":"homeHandler registers onEvent on deviceLink.events when the lazy handler is built, which happens before call() relays the first method to the app. Only a page that subscribes with on() and never calls a read hears nothing; the contract comment (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts:367-371) already says events start after the first home call.","kind":"comment","references":"8c0474a591dec873f4f12c9de344c24d360108999d04787bba9ab82248bb9a52","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"7192452fc8f36250b016a6e88a47f12adf39e460838d9f0de59ecc0ad0b50eca"},"summary":"Not user-visible for a home page that reads first: the handler's event listener is added before its first call is relayed, so a page that calls apps()/makes()/unread() at start and subscribes with on() misses no change after that read","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/webkit.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:33:07.654833Z","id":"6e455ccebd3ece3c2c1e74668d17e6f2bbf70893d4224d1deede4386189b99cb","body":{"detail":"The app's DeviceHost decides from Geolocator's LocationAccuracyStatus (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart preciseFix), but on iOS the shell reads navigator.geolocation, which says nothing about reduced accuracy. view() therefore snaps any fix of 2000 m or worse to its cell and marks it precise: false, and passes a better one through as precise. A cold GPS fix worse than 2 km under full accuracy is coarsened needlessly; a reduced-accuracy fix iOS reports under 2 km would pass as precise. Unverified on a device with Precise Location off.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"abc4b0a96b3b2145cdd51d552f22e73494887d946cb6340da2bed4a1de0b78fe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the grant answer carry the app's accuracy status (Geolocator.getLocationAccuracy, asking requestTemporaryFullAccuracy for a precise grant) and decide from it.","summary":"On iOS a precise grant's fix counts as precise only when its accuracy is under MIN_ACCURACY (2000 m); the system's reduced accuracy is inferred, not read","tags":["ios","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/webkit.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:33:07.655068Z","id":"846e6d717808f1c564b2863db66da16ad64ab36b1db68e60c6e66bd98b137b6b","body":{"detail":"pickFile settles only on the input's change or cancel event. WebKit fires cancel when the person closes the picker (Safari 16.4+), but closing the simulator's file menu could not be driven from XCUITest (a coordinate tap outside the menu left it open, target/ios/shots/t18-c1.png), so the cancelled path is covered only by web/shell/src/caps/device.test.ts with a synthetic cancel event.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"9bbd7140e67f399ba7026d44f5472e02b8a4d6e916a3ca306a227ce51b1da065"},"suggested_fix":"Check on a device that closing the Photo Library / Take Photo / Choose File menu and the photo picker each reject cancelled; if one does not, also settle on the window's next focus after the picker.","summary":"A WebKit picker that fires neither change nor cancel leaves the page's call pending for the document's life","tags":["ios","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/device.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:33:07.655190Z","id":"a6bc93c8586f5c78fce389721d7b7563e69f99b86de669991e8d44dd1e1cb9b7","body":{"detail":"navigator.geolocation in the shell's document makes WKWebView ask once per load: '\"127.0.0.1\" would like to use your current location' (target/ios/shots/t18-location-prompt-2.png), after Clax's grant dialog and iOS's 'Allow \"Clax\" to use your location?'. The person answers three questions on the first call, one naming an address. webview_flutter 4.x exposes no geolocation decision on iOS (WKUIDelegate's requestGeolocationPermissionFor... is not wrapped).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"9d525395402feac7f6127e87ca4937d35cda1dc745d03cca8b8c735f9c854cf1"},"suggested_fix":"Answer WebKit's geolocation request in the Runner (a WKUIDelegate decision granting the loopback shell origin, since Clax's per-app grant has already been asked), through a webview_flutter_wkwebview overlay.","summary":"On iOS WebKit's own location prompt names the shell's origin, \"127.0.0.1\", after Clax's grant and iOS's app prompt","tags":["ios","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/device.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:33:07.655237Z","id":"60c4c0bbc8c47d247f68a0b4e6c42da5b2dc3db0760121114c5c5279c8a9a823","body":{"detail":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts Device.Location.watch says Clax shows a location pill while a watch runs. On iOS the shell runs the watch (caps/webkit.ts Watches) and the app's DeviceView.watching stays 0, so only iOS's own status-bar location arrow shows (target/ios/shots/t18-location-result.png). The watch still ends with stopped when the app hides the view (deviceLink.hidden).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"76385160575ec1c149fce69f8fd970527eea58fabe0db10d9000634094d8fa75"},"suggested_fix":"Post the shell's running-watch count to the app (a host message) so app_screen.dart draws the pill and its tap stops them, or reword the contract for iOS.","summary":"iOS shows no Clax location pill for a watch WebKit runs: the app does not know it runs","tags":["ios","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/device.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:33:07.655349Z","id":"c49f162c60f0176b837b713fbdf23ad73415ca91c07f45a70ba6ba5ce4e6cfcb","body":{"detail":"deviceLink.platform is set by init({nonce, platform}) (web/shell/src/app/host.ts); a call made earlier is queued and posted to the app as the call itself, and apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart gives iOS's DeviceHost no share, file, camera or location port. Calls need the person's tap, which normally comes after init, so this is a narrow window.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"9d525395402feac7f6127e87ca4937d35cda1dc745d03cca8b8c735f9c854cf1"},"suggested_fix":"Hold the WebKit-capable calls made before init until init names the platform.","summary":"A device call made before the app's init on iOS goes to the app's native path, which there answers unavailable","tags":["ios","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/grants.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:06:01.590683Z","id":"48bdb9b513f68c058740d79a1a2f39b960fbb26af658d72ecd3607e265cbc493","body":{"detail":"ALWAYS (web/shell/src/caps/grants.ts:20) labels the prompts of grants (an Allow is written to localStorage, grants.ts request), sample (caps/sample.ts saves the daemon's sample-grant on Allow), net (caps/net.ts PUTs net-grants) and cross-read (caps/cross-read.ts PUTs db-grants). web/shell/src/app/native.ts maps askAnswer(id, \"always\") to the same \"allow\" those paths store. So a native prompt (apps/clax_app, ask in AskMsg.always) that shows an unchecked \"Always for this app\" box and answers allow still keeps the grant across views: the box's unchecked state does not mean \"this time only\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"517a891612d6057a359ec7e4b190b7defd4f96002b99cdb06ef1195b2ed8be0b"},"suggested_fix":"Either make a plain Allow last for the view only where an always choice is offered (and keep the grant only on always), or drop the always label and let the app show no checkbox.","summary":"The \"always\" choice a prompt offers changes nothing in the shell: every prompt that carries it already keeps a plain Allow","tags":["status:needs-decision","design","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:06:01.591323Z","id":"31bedb650b68356a7274b71bb6f0b395d0c9f0065a8de0495d3f4dc6d1dcb8e0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: a dismissed db.artifact(id) prompt refuses that read only and the next read asks again; cross-read.test.ts \"a dismissed prompt rejects that read and keeps no refusal: the next read asks again\" passes (bazelisk test //web:unit --test_arg=shell/src/caps). The app's native prompt answers askAnswer(id, \"dismiss\") into the same path (web/shell/src/app/native.ts). The change is in the shell's cross-read, so the browser's dialog, whose Escape and outside click also answer dismiss (ui/PromptDialog.svelte), asks again too.","supersedes":"44415b8019adb146027a3212e7d0baa2bff4da3e64410a6d1c46acd767d5882e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/sample.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:37:01.369772Z","id":"b5dc04c01778a92b501c6aca4b5153228c194c21806b142010ac8e5ea70585a1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"295a31f61e5b2b0551c128efd4bd83022fa20dd5760aa9bd1418d270358730b0","summary":"In the app the sample consent no longer goes through the shell's dialog: the app declares ask native (nativeOverlays, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart), the shell posts the prompt as an ask message, and AppScreen draws it with AskPrompt (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/ask_prompt.dart, f1c07f346b12). Widget tests cover the native prompt (//apps/clax_app:ui_ask_prompt_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_ask_test); no device or app run has shown it yet, so the chromeless app-mode half stays unverified.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/registry.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:20:14.518903Z","id":"50db751363ffdd5f4f29a6a3131e3ce387656a2a6b520f9fa7e3c701526d7f0b","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844 the artifact handler is a lazyHandler (web/shell/src/caps/lazy.ts:21-24): the page's first call awaits import(\"./artifact\") and only then runs frameGestureStrict (web/shell/src/caps/artifact.ts:114), which reads navigator.userActivation.isActive, focus in the frame and the time since the latest shell input at that moment. Before, the check ran a microtask after the message arrived (caps/host.ts:147-163 awaits only the resolved env). Two consequences on a view's first artifact call: (1) the viewer's click in the page is refused when the chunk load outlasts the click's transient activation (5 s) or the viewer gives the shell any input while it loads; the page is told rate_limited with NO_GESTURE, 'never on load or a timer', which is wrong for a click, and a second click works (the chunk is then loaded). Loads that slow are unlikely on a loopback daemon but possible on the hosted site over a poor network and in the app over the scheme handler (spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 4.2), and a failed load answers capability_disabled. (2) A call made with no gesture (on load, on a timer) is judged by a click the viewer gives the page while the chunk loads; that stays inside the residual gesture.ts:128-131 already names. No test covers a first publish whose chunk is slow. The device and home handlers (the lazy device chunk: device.ts:105, home.ts:111) have the same shape for the composer tier.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":17},"content_hash":"55f87e149c07f719001f4e7d11165f92a0a946dc6b348f291d3409e2fc718f3e"},"suggested_fix":"Judge the gesture before the await: frameGestureStrict is already in the artifact entry (comments.ts imports it), so lazyHandler can take an optional synchronous precheck(method, args) that the artifact registry entry sets to the strict check for publish (artifact.ts keeps its own as a second check), or the shell can import the chunk after first paint when the artifact declares artifact. Add a unit case: a publish whose chunk resolves after the activation has lapsed is still accepted.","summary":"artifact.publish's strict gesture is judged when the artifact chunk has loaded, not when the call arrived","tags":["review","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/registry.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:14:22.856339Z","id":"87d88025e61fd3147ed4e55e687f844a1eab2e8dd99a55faef1df6a622358ba1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: lazyHandler takes the handler's gesture tier (registry.ts: strictAtArrival for artifact, composerAtArrival for the device capabilities and home), judges it before awaiting the chunk, and passes the verdict to the loaded handler. web/shell/src/caps/registry.test.ts holds each chunk's load behind a gate: a publish judged ok at arrival passes though the activation lapsed before the load, a publish with no gesture (or with shell input just before it) is refused though the viewer clicks during the load, and share.text and home.openInbox are judged at arrival the same way. vitest run shell/src/caps/registry.test.ts: 4 passed; each failed before the fix.","supersedes":"50db751363ffdd5f4f29a6a3131e3ce387656a2a6b520f9fa7e3c701526d7f0b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:35.253381Z","id":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","body":{"detail":"addPageComment builds `new ApiError(res.status, msg)` with no code, while `mapped` (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:136-148) turns a 403 into the transient `unavailable` only when `e.code === \"spectator\"` (the daemon's SPECTATOR_CODE, crates/clax-core/src/seats.rs:51). createThread, sendToAgent and the other thread helpers go through `ok` in web/shell/src/threads.ts:51-59, which keeps `error.code`, so `create` maps the same refusal correctly and `reply` does not. The `seated()` check up front covers a view that already knows it is a spectator, but a seat lost between that check and the POST (the seat pool is the daemon's) reaches `mapped` with code null and is reported as a permanent `forbidden`, telling the page the viewer may never reply. addPageComment also duplicates `ok`'s body otherwise.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"13eec3cb0933daaae46aece6e47bcda0f5dab22726fe34c31b575ad61effe84c"},"suggested_fix":"Move addPageComment into web/shell/src/threads.ts beside addComment and have it return through `ok` (or parse `error.code` and pass it as ApiError's third argument), so every page write maps refusals by the daemon's code.","summary":"A page's comments.reply drops the daemon's error code, so a spectator's refused reply rejects 'forbidden' instead of 'unavailable'","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:35.988206Z","id":"114118c745a87e1c14f21e7dac3f822c668dce30b3c644118e3ebf056c391eb7","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:605-608 parses only error.message and throws `new ApiError(res.status, msg)`; ApiError's code defaults to null (web/shell/src/api.ts:63). The reply path (comments.ts:355) runs it through request -> mapped (comments.ts:272), and mapped yields `unavailable` only for `e.status === 403 && e.code === \"spectator\"` (comments.ts:142), else `forbidden` (comments.ts:143). threads.ts `ok` (web/shell/src/threads.ts:51-59) does parse error.code. The daemon refuses the comment route with 403 spectator: crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs calls clax_http::seats::require_seat on every thread write route (lines 737, 985, 1242, 1420, 1500, 1642, 1702), which returns spectator_refusal (crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs:67-72, code clax_core::seats::SPECTATOR_CODE). The up-front seated() check (comments.ts:203-205) only covers a view already marked spectating. Kind concern is right: a misclassified error code in a race, not a merge blocker.","kind":"comment","references":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","summary":"confirmed: addPageComment throws ApiError without the daemon's code, so mapped reports a seat lost before a reply as forbidden","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:24:50.505485Z","id":"4f50b36f30a2af57285106804f70a2455881a668cef0caff63f044c3ea9029a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f309a4046","summary":"Fixed: comments.reply goes through threads.ts addComment(viaPage) and keeps the daemon's error code; caps/comments.test.ts 'a reply the daemon refuses a spectator is unavailable, not forbidden' passes; //web:unit passes.","supersedes":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:43:10.915163Z","id":"8c34f9852ccb55201ee49b13b2fe7cbbe1af4a526e3cf9cd522f111ec5d251b9","body":{"detail":"noteShellInput clears tabAt after TAB_MS (500 ms) with setTimeout, while the module's other timing rules use after() from ../clock, which the browser tests advance. On a loaded machine a Tab's focus move into the frame can take longer than 500 ms of real time, so the browser tests that Tab into the page judge a real-time window.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":243},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"97912f85dbc2a790cf42c3778086c1482ce59143b1a718316269657fb624aa9f"},"suggested_fix":"Use after(TAB_MS, ...) from ../clock, as the hole opening does.","summary":"The Tab window (TAB_MS) runs on a real setTimeout, not the shell's clock","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649935Z","id":"f10658868c3102f9555de1fadcb1b806abc8fbb81c3f46f4cc36bf775b22d26e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"94ab5cdaf4de5bbed63a3fac96b1c4d50f4102b26fc9a41c5430dbdc8a8c63ea","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"755f77437e4c357f9c227a909b248314d87a2588d394fbdfe8c65d3a5fbd33f8"},"summary":"The server now computes these facts: a site host's GET /_clax/api/whoami answers {kind: owner|person|guest|link|visitor, id?, name?, level, can_edit} for the site's caller (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs whoami; test crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_api.rs whoami_names_the_caller). This closes once the bridge's user capability reads it instead of the shell token (Task 9 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md).","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/room.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T18:09:13.419864Z","id":"bf6771c4f4f33bda8fb711387aa6848d2752f076b97cc3aa2dd67e9b92f39d20","body":{"detail":"Rooms::claim refuses a label held by another viewer (crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs), so the shell's reconnect after its viewer changes is closed 4403 peer_taken and reconnects after RECONNECT_MS[0] under a new label, while the retired socket stays until the new one opens. Peers see the old label leave and a new one enter, not a seamless rename.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"f4ed1e6f9b00a97f4fd10591d7bd7ae78847bec268aeebcf089dde41989d7ed2"},"summary":"A viewer change on a hosted Clax (a visitor becoming a guest) now costs the room a leave and an enter under a fresh label","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284551Z","id":"be4349abc3bb34bc60dd7520372beb7273f130632211a9f97207265e179f28a3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2589fda3","summary":"The user capability's facts about the viewer now come from the site's GET /_clax/api/whoami in the bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts userLocals), never the shell token: isOwner is kind == owner, canEdit is can_edit, can() follows level; the shell's user handler answers only profiles and search (web/shell/src/caps/user.ts). Evidence: just web-test passes //web:unit (181 files, 1855 tests), including web/bridge/test/origin.test.ts 'answers who the viewer is from the site's whoami, never from a shell token' (a person with publish rights canEdit and is not the owner; a guest neither) and web/shell/src/caps/user.test.ts 'answers only the lookups: the viewer's own facts are the bridge's'; crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_api.rs whoami_names_the_caller passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__4 --test_arg=site_api: 11 passed).","supersedes":"94ab5cdaf4de5bbed63a3fac96b1c4d50f4102b26fc9a41c5430dbdc8a8c63ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/room.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.303793Z","id":"71bc09932c01d5425aa47681e6066f16bf2d763f3f4a1174883e9709a9f2fffa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2589fda3","summary":"Obsolete: the shell's room handler is gone (2589fda3). The page's room socket is the bridge's, on its site's /_clax/api/room (web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts), one label per document with no reconnect on a viewer change, so a viewer change no longer costs peers a leave and an enter.","supersedes":"bf6771c4f4f33bda8fb711387aa6848d2752f076b97cc3aa2dd67e9b92f39d20","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/room.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.383133Z","id":"9a33e5917b175a42a38dd6c8d1ad5200c0e887e785db5a7e68a3847fa287f99f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"71bc09932c01d5425aa47681e6066f16bf2d763f3f4a1174883e9709a9f2fffa","summary":"Correction: the reconnect on a viewer change is kept (da123eb6). The bridge's room socket reopens under the same label at the new level when the framing shell reports a viewer change (room.watch and room/viewer, web/shell/src/caps/room.ts) or, top-level, when the site's whoami changed as the page comes back into view (web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts renamed). A label another viewer holds (4403 peer_taken) still takes a fresh one, so a viewer change on a hosted Clax can still cost peers a leave and an enter. Tests: web/bridge/test/room-socket.test.ts 'reopens under the same label when a framing shell reports a viewer change' and 'top-level, reopens at the new level when the site's whoami changed'.","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.420365Z","id":"b16085a50453a1a900109507867afffda0f4f04987b23ec802100811e79654bd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"be4349abc3bb34bc60dd7520372beb7273f130632211a9f97207265e179f28a3","summary":"guest is covered too (da123eb6): the viewer's own profile entry has guest: true exactly when whoami's kind is guest, framed or not (web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts userLocals markGuest), and can() resolves null when whoami could not be read. Test: web/bridge/test/origin.test.ts 'asks a framing shell for other people's names, and names only the viewer without one' (the guest cases) and 'without the declaration only the universal members answer'; just web-test passes //web:unit (182 files, 1863 tests).","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.590583Z","id":"7ba3f19bd5164f6462f8efe0b59e48aafc7eff43a560159315a77cb1f7f29260","body":{"detail":"commentable() (lines 238-243, called from opening() and post() at line 389) and the comments_off branch of mapped (line 171) have no test: commenting out all three leaves //web:unit and //web:typecheck green under `just web-test`; only //web:lint fails, on the now-unused commentable declaration. A page could then open the composer or post while the switch is off and get `forbidden` (permanent) instead of `unavailable` from the daemon's 403. Nor does any test cover ArtifactController.refused turning the view's comments off on a refused reply or pick (artifact-controller.ts saveThread and submitDraft).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"fea78d32c2c2506bae58ae067380260b5abc290eac5c1a1128acabc5f3b9291e"},"suggested_fix":"Add caps tests: with env.commentsOff returning true, composer open and create/reply reject unavailable with no fetch; a 403 {code: comments_off} maps to unavailable. Add a controller test that a reply refused comments_off disables Comment.","summary":"No test covers the page capability's comments-off gate or its comments_off mapping","tags":["app-push","tests","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.542989Z","id":"80f69165ee0cae8c745a9384882b3f27f5fd731b9f737023a198a7e0f229c671","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb64b9d4","summary":"Tests added: caps/comments.test.ts 'while comments are off the page opens no composer and posts nothing, and still resolves' (fails with commentable() made a no-op) and 'a comment the daemon refuses comments_off is unavailable, not forbidden' (fails with the comments_off branch of mapped removed); topbar.test.ts 'a reply refused comments_off says so and turns comments off in the view' (fails with ArtifactController.refused not calling noteComments). just web-test: //web:unit, typecheck, lint, bundle_size PASSED; just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6b.log). ","supersedes":"7ba3f19bd5164f6462f8efe0b59e48aafc7eff43a560159315a77cb1f7f29260","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.853096Z","id":"fa62d3000976bf0f33c6ddc48e104580ffcea2ccb7e51ea8265ac9c3695e2989","body":{"detail":"noteShellInput clears tabAt after TAB_MS (500 ms) with setTimeout, while the module's other timing rules use after() from ../clock, which the browser tests advance. On a loaded machine a Tab's focus move into the frame can take longer than 500 ms of real time, so the browser tests that Tab into the page judge a real-time window.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":264},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"97912f85dbc2a790cf42c3778086c1482ce59143b1a718316269657fb624aa9f"},"suggested_fix":"Use after(TAB_MS, ...) from ../clock, as the hole opening does.","summary":"The Tab window (TAB_MS) runs on a real setTimeout, not the shell's clock","supersedes":"8c34f9852ccb55201ee49b13b2fe7cbbe1af4a526e3cf9cd522f111ec5d251b9","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:10:11.242748Z","id":"672116804ecbdcba5cf89fa949232adb5aa1db3bae3dbae33ead01f0c270b6a7","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts is now 67 lines and holds only grantRead (the db.grant consent); no shell code holds db.artifact(id) subscriptions or subscribes docs:<B>?reader=<A>. Those subscriptions live in the bridge's dbTransport (web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts), where a page's own and another app's subscriptions share one MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS (64) per view, first reads still pending included (held and full in origin.ts), and are refetched from the page's own site. Evidence: web/bridge/test/origin.test.ts 'holds at most MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS subscriptions of other apps, however many are asked for at once' (200 at once: 64 fulfilled, 136 resource_exhausted, and the page's own subscribe refused while they are pending) and 'drops a subscribe still waiting on its first read when it is unsubscribed or subscribed again' pass in bazel test //web:unit.","kind":"comment","references":"987f6cee41694dc9159b8de6b5802bf64b228f61e338ffffa65037ea521af7d9","summary":"Proposed close (obsolete): the shell holds no subscriptions any more, and the bridge counts both kinds against one cap","tags":["proposal:close","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
